==Spanish==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|VL.|es}} *''nascere'', from {{etyl|la|es}} {{term|nāscī|lang=la}}, present active infinitive of {{term|nāscor|lang=la}}, from earlier {{m|la|gnāscor}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|es}} {{m|ine-pro|*genh₁-}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/na.ˈθeɾ/|lang=es}} (''Spain'')
* {{IPA|/na.ˈseɾ/|lang=es}} (''Latin America'')

===Verb===
{{es-verb|nac|er|pres=nazco|part=nacido}}

# to [[be born]], to [[sprout]], to begin to grow; to hatch (out)
# to [[grow]]; to [[rise]], to have its source (river); to [[rise]] (sun); to have its roots

